{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall boil.</b> I explained it as referring to fire, and likewise \"and they boiled the Passover in fire.\" It mentioned \"and you shall boil\" so that one not eat it raw." "<b>And you shall turn in the morning.</b> The disputants say that one may go on the holy day to his house and land. But we do not rely on our own reasoning regarding commandments, but rather on the transmitters of the Torah. Now we find: \"on the eighth day he sent the people\" — and it is a holy day. And afterward it is written: \"on the twenty-third day of the seventh month he sent the people.\" Some say the meaning is \"to your tents,\" as it is, and on the weekday to his land." "<b>And you shall go to your tents.</b> A circuit around Jerusalem, and from there he goes to his land on the weekday."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:41.145044253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}